<p>Ubersuggest Site Audit provides a guided technical check inside the wider Ubersuggest platform. It can help a site owner create an initial issue list, but the list still needs URL-level verification and business context before it becomes an implementation plan.</p>

<h2 id="what-is-ubersuggest">What Is Ubersuggest?</h2>

<p><a href="https://neilpatel.com/ubersuggest/" rel="noopener noreferrer">The official Ubersuggest page</a> lists Site Audit alongside keyword research, competitive research, rank tracking and backlink features. This makes it a broad search workflow rather than a dedicated desktop crawler.</p>

<h2 id="site-audit-features">What the Site Audit Is For</h2>

<p>Use the audit to locate reported SEO and code conditions on crawled pages and to establish a first technical backlog. Before choosing it, verify the current crawl allowance, project history, rendering behaviour, exports and scheduling in the live account or vendor documentation.</p>

<h2 id="running-an-audit">Run an Audit</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Enter the canonical site address and confirm the intended host and scope.</li>
  <li>Run the crawl and compare the discovered page count with your sitemap and known important URLs.</li>
  <li>Open each priority category and inspect representative affected URLs.</li>
  <li>Group repeated findings by template or shared component.</li>
  <li>Retest changed pages and confirm the intended result in Search Console where indexing is involved.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="interpreting-results">Interpret the Results</h2>

<p>An automated label cannot tell whether a redirect, noindex, canonical or short page is intentional. Record the observed condition and intended state before recommending a fix. Use <a href="https://search.google.com/search-console/about" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Search Console</a> for Google's own indexing and search-performance data, and a browser or performance tool for page behaviour.</p>

<h2 id="ubersuggest-vs-alternatives">Ubersuggest vs Alternatives</h2>

<p>Ubersuggest fits a guided, broad SEO workflow. For a free crawl of up to 500 URLs, consider <a href="/website-audit-tools/screaming-frog/">Screaming Frog</a>. For a verified site's recurring cloud crawl, consider <a href="/website-audit-tools/ahrefs/">Ahrefs Free</a>. Use the <a href="/website-audit-tools/">tool directory</a> to filter by task and access model.</p>

<h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2>

<p>Ubersuggest advertises both limited free access and paid access, including lifetime offers, but terms and limits can change. Check the <a href="https://app.neilpatel.com/en/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer">official pricing page</a> for the current site-audit allowance, projects, users, billing term and refund conditions.</p>

<p><small>Product facts checked against Ubersuggest's official product and pricing pages on 11 September 2026.</small></p>

</ContentLayout>
